data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Work with $m = \\min(p, 1-p)$, which lies in $(0, \\tfrac12]$, and use $\\operatorname{logit}(p) = \\pm g(m)$\nwith $g(m) = \\log\\dfrac{1-m}{m}$. Write $g$ as $\\log(1 - m) - \\log(m)$ for very small $m$. Near\n$m = \\tfrac12$, write $g(m) = \\operatorname{log1p}\\!\\left(\\dfrac{1-2m}{m}\\right)$. The subtraction $1 - 2m$ is\nexact for $m$ in $[\\tfrac14, \\tfrac12]$."},"hints_note":null}

